  "symptomOrConditionMarkers": {
    "$comment": "Surface cues that a clause reports a symptom or bodily state rather than narrator voice. Used for ONE purpose: deciding whether a first-person pronoun in a clause alongside a baby clause is a second patient or just the person telling the story. 'Em lo qua, be bo bu' names a worried mother, not an unwell one. Deliberately GENEROUS: a missed marker keeps the message CONFLICTED, which costs a clarification round; a false marker would silently drop a mother's symptom. When in doubt the list should over-match. Never used to create a target on its own.",
